        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, most roofs last between 15 and 30 years for asphalt shingles, and 40 to 100 years for metal, tile, or slate. High-elevation mountain areas (like Heber City) experience heavier snow loads and stronger freeze-thaw cycles than lower valleys, which can wear down materials faster .",
